1
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:10,290
(Sheldon:)A hush falls over the crowd
as Cooper studies the board.

2
00:00:11,602 --> 00:00:13,232
(Sheldon:)He makes his move.

3
00:00:13,404 --> 00:00:16,734
(Sheldon:)He's dividing both sides by I,
he's adding back the coefficient.

4
00:00:16,907 --> 00:00:19,307
(Sheldon:)He has a value for P.
He's plugging that back in.

5
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:21,940
(Sheldon:)He takes the derivative
and he solves the equation.

6
00:00:22,113 --> 00:00:25,813
- Crowd goes wild. "Nobel, Nobel!"
- Cooper.

7
00:00:26,817 --> 00:00:28,747
"Nobel." Kripke.

8
00:00:30,321 --> 00:00:32,381
Yeah... Don't look at my board.

9
00:00:34,158 --> 00:00:37,758
- What's that?
- That's a drawing of a really cool train.

10
00:00:37,928 --> 00:00:39,828
Yeah, don't look at that, either.

11
00:00:40,030 --> 00:00:42,230
(Sheldon:)- What do you want?
- I have some bad news.

12
00:00:42,399 --> 00:00:45,299
You're working on a grant proposal
for a new fusion reactor.

13
00:00:45,469 --> 00:00:48,299
I'm working on a grant proposal
for a new fusion reactor.

14
00:00:48,472 --> 00:00:51,932
The university is only allowed
to submit one proposal.

15
00:00:52,109 --> 00:00:56,269
(Sheldon:)So they asked you to pack up your things
and ship out. That's hard cheese, Barry.

16
00:00:56,447 --> 00:00:58,537
(Sheldon:)You're one of the good ones.

17
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:02,310
(Kripke:)No, they're making us work together.

